  "labelled": [
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C34-01, TASK-AC-C021DADA60B8",
      "text": "A ladder whose rounds nobody has marked yet reads \"No rounds marked yet\" (live count and the log's count), not \"0 of N rounds completed\": nothing stated is not zero; an explicit zero still reads \"0 of N\"."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C60-01, AC-R014-01, AC-R014-02",
      "text": "Undo finish · resume ladder keeps its quiet style, its control height and the small button's own inline padding (`var(--spacing-300)`, so its focus frame clears the first letter); its row gives that padding back outside the box with a negative inline margin (`calc(var(--spacing-300) * -1)`), so its text starts at the rounds-completed count's left edge."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-R013-01, AC-R013-03, TASK-AC-C021DADA60B8",
      "text": "The ladder log asks each movement's next-round amount only once a round is stated (zero included): with nothing stated there is no \"Completed in round 1\" field."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-R013-01",
      "text": "A tap inside the live check-off's selection leaves only the rounds before it (the log tiles' rule), where it used to select through it."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "JOURNEY-012 (readable wrapping), AC-R013-02",
      "text": "A live round tile keeps the read-only tile's declared inset (`var(--spacing-200)`) instead of the Chip's wider inline inset, which broke BURPEE mid-word (BURPE/E) in the three-column grid at 390. Size, type, frame and selection are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-30138C4A2AFF (owner decision 2026-11-16, Decision 2)",
      "text": "At a narrow phone width (22.5rem and below; here 320 px) a round tile's inset is tightened from `var(--spacing-200)` to `var(--spacing-100)`, so the twelve-round grid fits one 320×568 screen before Start (544 px, was 592). The column rule, gap, frame, the frame's own inset and type are unchanged; at 390 nothing changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C33-01, AC-R013-02",
      "text": "A live round's toggle fills its grid cell and starts its words at its top, as a read-only round does, so a row's tiles and round labels stay level when one tile's words fit one line and its neighbour's wrap (a one- and a two-digit timed rung at 320 px). The accepted states' rows hold alike words, so nothing drawn changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-105",
      "criterion": "AC-C35-01, AC-R012-01, TASK-AC-F3CDA21AC50B",
      "text": "The prescription reads the shared `state/ladder.ts` readings (Review's too): each round is also said in words to a screen reader (visually hidden), live toggles describe their round's work, and the summary line wraps a long word rather than overflowing. No drawn word or box changes for the accepted push up and burpee ladder."
    }
  ],
